7-2869bffc442f" :question/math-academy-id "q-141113" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2y}{x},\\,y(2)=-1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=-1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=-1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{{2}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{A}{4} \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141113/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141113"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-141114/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "aa80debc-bf73-5dee-b7f3-16746495d52f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141114/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "0ff10567-e99b-581f-9a5c-3d8134aec462" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141114/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "57167bc3-7525-5a98-8e9c-f60d49407684" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141114/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "c7d131b7-f132-532b-9637-35c5693ffaad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141114/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "04f7c9cb-03bb-5f4a-bc2c-dac592eecf5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-141114/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e09e87c1-7fa9-5e7e-867d-2744524684a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-141114/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-141114/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-141114/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-141114/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-141114/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-141114/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-141114" :question/id #uuid "a8e92955-2aba-5ce5-9cc9-92df3e501cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-141114" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{x},\\,y(-1)=3.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=Ax$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=Ax$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-1)=3.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(-1)=3$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =Ax \\\\ 3 & =A(-1) \\\\ 3 & =-A \\\\ A & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-3x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-141114/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-141114"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352654/field-1/80be74dd3655fc061aa59382e93baef1436a20b0813d3492b166b5e4258519f8" :answer/id #uuid "e46a7ae1-4011-5704-af42-e13cf11c2581" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5e^{-6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352654/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "98285775-a9fb-56b7-be3d-393fa624d3e8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352654/field-1/80be74dd3655fc061aa59382e93baef1436a20b0813d3492b166b5e4258519f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-352654/field-1/80be74dd3655fc061aa59382e93baef1436a20b0813d3492b166b5e4258519f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352654" :question/id #uuid "234ff426-43d9-539a-9bed-18f994374c5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-352654" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3y,\\,y(2)=5.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{e}^{3x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We're given that $y=A{e}^{3x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=5.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=5$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{e}^{3x} \\\\ 5 & =A{e}^{3\\cdot 2} \\\\ 5 & =A{e}^{6} \\\\ \\frac{5}{{e}^{6}} & =A \\\\ A & =\\frac{5}{{e}^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-352654/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82a9b23c-4c79-56cd-9761-79d0ee22646d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352654"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
